{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings","id":575469,"title":"Why I feel like Backgrounds are the primary criteria for Seemings","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-01T12:30:15-07:00","id":575469,"title":"Why I feel like Backgrounds are the primary criteria for Seemings","content":"For me at least; there's three primary factors.<br /> <br /> Firstly the choice of headers, &quot;Background&quot; appears as a header in many WoD Splat write ups. However this is the first and only time it's been used for an &quot;iconic example&quot; - compare the Background header in the 1E Seemings. The same for the header &quot;Escape&quot;; it makes me think of similar Splat specific headers like 1E Seeming's &quot;Durance&quot; or Threshold's &quot;Geists&quot;. Those sections were not iconic examples but broad overviews. I naturally read this WoD book in the context of the previous WoD books I read; which leads me to think the highly-specific Background section is for most Changelings and not just one iconic example.<br /> <br /> <br /> Secondly the way the background flows into the durance, which flows into the escape. The escape That makes perfect sense for an iconic example. If you're the apex of Wizenedness it makes sense your key life events are all Wizenedly - but the iconic example is also the only example in the seeming text; and it uses terms like &quot;Before the Durance, many Wizened&quot; - which while clearly stating that it's not all Wizened - also clearly state that it is not one single example.<br /> <br /> The example's pomimence and it's explicit plurality gives me an impression that the iconic example is also the default example; and in the default example the Escape flows directly from the Background.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thirdly it's just the complete and utter lack of any discussion for an Escape which doesn't have it's roots in your mortal life. There's nothing about escapes based on your Keeper's weaknesses. Nothing about escapes based on a random opportunity opening up. There's nothing about escapes that come from your Kith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T13:22:37-07:00","id":575538,"title":"","content":"Well, it seems like one thing they're going for is the idea that people don't (usually) wind up in Faerie entirely by accident. Sort of like earthy predators, it appears that the True Fae make the weakened and isolated their prey. Many beasts already felt trapped and powerless in their lives before the Durance; many Darklings were betrayed and cast adrift; many Fairest were tormented by the feeling that they had wasted their lives; many Ogres were pushed to the limits of sanity by bullying; many Elementals have had their delusions of grandeur shattered; and many Wizened pushed their lives aside in favor of their work or passion, and yet were unsatisfied.<br /> <br /> I think anyone could still be taken, but they won't generally be taken out of the blue. The Fae wait until they suffer a moment of weakness, or are cut loose from the things that gave their life stability. Therefore, it's this tragedy, whatever it is, that comes to define their relationship with Faerie and, by extension, their means of escape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T13:46:34-07:00","id":575557,"title":"","content":"I see an issue here in that, as currently written, that weakness is what ends up defining the character. The message here seems to be that if you have a particular character flaw you will be taken (because some people are more likely to be or some personality types tend that way, however it was said earlier), and because of it you have one means of escape. It seems a single weakness ends up defining more than just the eventual trend of the character (who I am playing when the game starts) but who they were to begin with. If anything, it Arcadia does not signal a serious change in the character as much as another step along their way to health. Maybe this is supposed to be the point, but what it effectively does is limit character options by enforcing a rigid code of history and psychological progression on the seemings.<br /> <br /> I love the idea of seeming being connected to how you found your strength, but I believe there is more room for players (as opposed to developers) to decide why that strength was needed. Or even, for that matter, the particular form it took to manifest, but that discussion has been gone into in depth earlier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5428,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5428-mr-feral","user":"Mr. Feral","date":". 07-01-2015, 04:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5428-mr-feral","name":"Mr. Feral","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5428_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T13:58:13-07:00","id":575597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=575538#post575538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it seems like one thing they're going for is the idea that people don't (usually) wind up in Faerie entirely by accident.</div> </div> </div> </div> If that's true then I think it's probably the worst possible decision that could ever be made.<br /> <br /> The <u>entire point</u> of a Seeming is that it represents how you reclaimed agency. Your Kith is what your Keeper made you, your Seeming is how you took back control.<br /> <br /> But if the Keeper chose you because you had a weakness*; if the Keeper chose you because you were a victim of bullying, and bullying victims become Ogres; then becoming an Ogre is no longer you taking control of the story. It's just the next chapter in the story someone else wrote for you. It completely torpedoes the theme of Seemings, and arguably the whole theme of Changeling being about abuse survivors taking control of their lives with it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> * (I'm ok with Keepers targeting people for weeknesses; but only if it's made clear that there's still multiple Seeming possibilties for each changeling. Someone who's a bullying victim might be more likely to become an Ogre; but only slightly more likely. And if their Kith is Maker or Artist then they're more likely to become Wizened than Ogres)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T14:36:54-07:00","id":575636,"title":"","content":"Well, I think there's more than one way to look at the &quot;moment&quot; of weakness thing.<br /> <br /> For one thing, the kinds of tragedy described in the different Seeming write-up are all, at least potentially, universal. Most if not all people have times in their lives where they feel trapped, or betrayed, or have doubts about their life choices, or experience bullying, or have their self-perceptions challenged, or experience dissatisfaction with something they're usually proud of or passionate about. A person doesn't have to be weak in character in order to experience these low points... the moment of weakness may only have been a momentary lapse if supernatural forces hadn't intervened.<br /> <br /> Likewise, because all of these things could have happened to an individual over their life, or even just in the time immediately leading up to their Durance, it's probably not easy to guess what seeming they'll end up being. The True Fey don't think like people, and time flows differently between Faerie and earth. Perhaps a Keeper sees a boy being bullied in school, but the boy isn't taken until after he's grown up and become a successful family man. The Keeper might try to keep him in line with the kind of bullying he suffered as a child, but his response may not be at all what the Keeper expects.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, Keepers almost certainly underestimate the people they capture, at least the ones that later escape. They see a weakness in someone that they think they can exploit for their own purposes, but overlook the strengths that would allow the Changeling to overcome those weaknesses. That's where agency comes in, I think: the weakness that your keeper saw in you defines the way they try to keep you in captivity, and it's by overcoming that weakness that one escapes. The response isn't always healthy, exactly but it demonstrates that the Changeling has learned from the thing that weakened them in the first place and has made the decision not to be a victim anymore.<br /> <br /> The Beast, having resolved to be caged no longer, finds the strength and determination to break free of his prison.<br /> The Darkling, once betrayed by those she depended on, learns to be self-reliant.<br /> The Fairest, sick of never living up to his potential, resolves to take control of his own destiny.<br /> The Ogre, having been wounded by life's cruelty, makes herself tough enough to overcome any suffering.<br /> The Elemental, his delusions shattered, lets go of his ego and opens himself to the wider world.<br /> The Wizened, unsatisfied with her work, refuses to give up and redoubles her efforts to improve.<br /> <br /> The Keeper decided how the story began when they took the Changeling, and the Changeling can't do anything about that. She can, however, take control and write her own ending, and thereby escape.<br /> <br /> I think this is the kind of thing they were going for, though I could be off base...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 07-01-2015, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T17:10:00-07:00","id":575782,"title":"","content":"Also bear in mind that we're dealing with a realm where the Wyrd dominates with its \u201cfated stories\u201d thing. I can definitely see the idea that nothing that happened to the changeling was accidental \u2014 that the Wyrd \u201cchose\u201d her to play a role in Arcadia because of who she was. And as with everything else with the Wyrd, this came with a Catch, represented by a Seeming: achieve the conditions of the Seeming, and she's free of the bonds holding her to Arcadia. <i>Not</i> part of the Wyrd's plans, as it were; but its own rules <i>require</i> it to include a backdoor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T17:21:03-07:00","id":575794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=575597#post575597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> * (I'm ok with Keepers targeting people for weeknesses; but only if it's made clear that there's still multiple Seeming possibilties for each changeling. Someone who's a bullying victim might be more likely to become an Ogre; but only slightly more likely. And if their Kith is Maker or Artist then they're more likely to become Wizened than Ogres)</div> </div> </div> </div>This will be made abundantly clear. A certain type of person is prone to certain responses, but you are allowed making that choice for yourself. Fate does not force you to escape in a certain way. As a player, you choose how your character responds. I'll include a sidebar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T21:07:41-07:00","id":576000,"title":"","content":"CatDoom has basically covered what I would have, but I want to elaborate on some bits.<br /> <br /> Someone who was betrayed might be primed to choose the Darkling or Ogre Seeming, but <i>how</i> were they betrayed? Was it because a mentor failed to allow them the opportunities to grow? That's the seeds of a Fairest or Wizened Seeming. Were they betrayed by the Man, or the System? They might choose to become a Beast instead. Were they betrayed because they deluded themselves into thinking they were the center of the universe? Deciding on an Elemental Seeming would work here.<br /> <br /> It depends entirely on what they choose to make of their backstory, and how they take their next step. If a couple of different Changelings agree to escape together, how does that play out for this once-betrayed protagonist? Does he focus on his betrayal and decide that, if it's me or him, I'll be the one to escape? Does he see another betrayal coming and steel himself against it, powering through and turning the tables on the traitor? Does he take charge of the others and get them to safety? Does he demonstrate his once-inhibited, now-flowering genius and <i>make</i> a way out? Does he violate the rules of decorum he once strongly believed in to slather mud all over himself for camouflage? Does he turn back when he comes across a reminder of how important his Keeper considers him?<br /> <br /> There's really only one backstory here, but there are six (and more) ways to interpret it. You look at it and ask, &quot;Where did all go wrong? What was my vulnerability that led to being betrayed here?&quot; Sure, it's easy to go with a generic, &quot;I was too trusting,&quot; but you only need to poke at it a bit more to get a dozen more answers to those questions that you could use.<br /> <br /> I really hope the Seemings get the standard set of Five Questions all the 2e x-splats have been getting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T22:33:28-07:00","id":576059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=576000#post576000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really hope the Seemings get the standard set of Five Questions all the 2e x-splats have been getting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mm? 'fraid I'm unfamiliar. Would you mind elaborating on these?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T22:37:52-07:00","id":576065,"title":"","content":"It's not my place to patronize or anything...<br /> <br /> But may I say how <i>freaking</i> disappointed I am with this thread?<br /> <br /> <i>How many god damned times has David been told this exact same damn thing</i><i>?</i> How many times has he responded with the same answer he's given here?<br /> <br /> A whole damn lot.<br /> <br /> I mean, hell, I saw him give the answer to this problem just this morning, <i>and this thread still exists</i>.<br /> <br /> Even if the changes were going to be made to this part of the text, and it's not, revisions take time. David and the writers have lives outside of this that keeps them busy, and they also have lots and lots of other projects to work on. That doesn't mean changes aren't being made, it's just not out.<br /> <br /> But more to the point, <i>David has answered this concern <b><u>six times now. At the least</u></b></i>.<br /> <br /> You know what's he's going to do and not do by now. If you don't, you're not reading. And if you are reading, you're being inconsiderate <i>at best</i>.<br /> <br /> Just.<br /> <br /> Gah.<br /> <br /> Continue. Just know that, for what it's worth, I'm disappointed this thread exists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T22:48:13-07:00","id":576070,"title":"","content":"In fairness, Arc, this thread only exists because Raven said he had specific reasons he felt Seeming was 90% determined by background, but didn't want to fill up the Wizened thread with more dead horse beating, I requested he PM his reasons to me because I was interested in hearing them, and then Gaius said he was interested too, and asked if we could just have the discussion in a different thread. We specifically created it so those of us who aren't fed up with this discussion yet have a place to conduct it that won't bother the people who are.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:red\">If you are not interested in this line of discussion, you are not obligated to read or post in this thread, but please don't come into it just to threadcrap.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-02-2015, 01:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T22:50:53-07:00","id":576072,"title":"","content":"I get that. It's just been stewing in my mind all day, and I couldn't quite get it out of my head. I needed to say something.<br /> <br /> Anyways, resume conversation. I've done my thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-02-2015, 01:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T23:24:12-07:00","id":576084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=576059#post576059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mm? 'fraid I'm unfamiliar. Would you mind elaborating on these?</div> </div> </div> </div>My memory is apparently crap. Werewolf 2e has a set of 5 questions for each Auspice under &quot;Making a Hunter&quot;. I thought that Vampire 2e also did, but I just checked and it's untrue. I also thought Mage 2e had'em and a quick glance at the Moros spoiler tells me this is untrue. GMC had a set of 5 questions for determining Integrity breaking points.<br /> <br /> Apparently I just got stuff muddled in my head.<br /> <br /> Summer is literally frying my brain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T23:59:55-07:00","id":576102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=575636#post575636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For one thing, the kinds of tragedy described in the different Seeming write-up are all, at least potentially, universal.<br /> <br /> Most if not all people have times in their lives where they feel trapped, or betrayed, or have doubts about their life choices, or experience bullying, or have their self-perceptions challenged, or experience dissatisfaction with something they're usually proud of or passionate about. A person doesn't have to be weak in character in order to experience these low points... the moment of weakness may only have been a momentary lapse if supernatural forces hadn't intervened.</div> </div> </div> </div> I see it differently. The way it's phrased and it's promimence in the write up makes me feel that it's not just a &quot;time in your life&quot; but a major charachter defining thing.<br /> <br /> An Ogre wasn't just bullied by one guy for a few days before the teacher put a stop to it. He was bullied, at a minimum, enough to have a permement effect upon his charachter and self image. Enough that he knew how to build armour when he reached Arcadia. Actually; that's explicit in the text -<br /> <br /> &quot;Ogres were first people who were pushed and pushed and hurt and hurt until they had no choice but to lash out, to respond with violence or brutality, and that moment, when they snapped&quot;<br /> <br /> I could agree that most people experienced bullying; but so much bullying that they felt the only response is violence or brutality. I wouldn't call that universal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=575782#post575782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also bear in mind that we're dealing with a realm where the Wyrd dominates with its \u201cfated stories\u201d thing. I can definitely see the idea that nothing that happened to the changeling was accidental \u2014 that the Wyrd \u201cchose\u201d her to play a role in Arcadia because of who she was. And as with everything else with the Wyrd, this came with a Catch, represented by a Seeming: achieve the conditions of the Seeming, and she's free of the bonds holding her to Arcadia. <i>Not</i> part of the Wyrd's plans, as it were; but its own rules <i>require</i> it to include a backdoor.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said. Your Seeming is how you make your Story <i>yours</i>. It would defeat the entire point if the True Fae or the Wyrd chose it for you. That still applies if the rules include Seemings as a backdoor.<br /> <br /> Choosing one of two forks in the road (Seeming or staying in arcadia) is not forging your own path.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=575794#post575794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This will be made abundantly clear. A certain type of person is prone to certain responses, but you are allowed making that choice for yourself. Fate does not force you to escape in a certain way. As a player, you choose how your character responds. I'll include a sidebar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really glad to hear it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T01:44:20-07:00","id":576219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=576102#post576102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Choosing one of two forks in the road (Seeming or staying in arcadia) is not forging your own path.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why?<br /> <br /> Besides a forced metaphor here (the Seeming is being treated as a set path rather than a forged path), it feels like you're just denying the basic premise of the game to an extent here. It feels a lot like your stance can be boiled down to, &quot;Changelings can't regain their own agency because once they were taken they were forced into a story and the moment of taking control of their own story is really just what the story scripted for them and is an illusion.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which really doesn't seem like an issue with the Seemings at all. It feels like you're rejecting the concept of regaining agency in this situation because some aspects of what occur to you and what you choose to do are heavily impacted by previous parts of your life. CtL doesn't really work if you take either a hard determinist or a complete existentialist stance on this. You seem to be reading the text from the former stance, and arguing against it from the latter stance; rather than doing both from a more compatibilist position (which is sort of necessary for a game that stresses both the power of determined stories, and the power to have agency to make meaningful changes to them).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T09:35:49-07:00","id":576492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=576219#post576219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &quot;Changelings can't regain their own agency because once they were taken they were forced into a story and the moment of taking control of their own story is really just what the story scripted for them and is an illusion.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not what I'm saying at all.<br /> <br /> In fact I'm saying the exact opposite. What I'm actually saying is that the Changeling book should make it extremely clear that gaining a Seeming is <b>not</b> what the story scripted for them; in order to make it possible for a Changeling to regain their own agency. And that I feel if backgrounds are tied too strongly into a Changeling's eventual seeming then it would make your Seeming into what the Story has Scripted for you.<br /> <br /> Fortunately MachineIV's promised a sidebar to address the issue <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T16:05:46-07:00","id":576872,"title":"","content":"There was a lot more to my post than just that, that I feel addresses most of your response preemptively.<br /> <br /> As well, you'll note I said, &quot;it feels like,&quot; this is what you're saying.<br /> <br /> In the end, I think the key point you're not really addressing is predetermination vs. free-will has a middle ground.<br /> <br /> Background has to impact Seeming, because without background, what defines the character's strengths and weaknesses that in turn define their frame of mind for their choice to escape? <br /> <br /> The issue really can't be that backgrounds are tied heavily into Seeming, because Seeming is so highly based on personality, which is something that comes from background. How do you get to the point of being ready to betray someone to escape your Durance without that part of your personality being there in your background? If your Durance is what makes you like that, then you're not reclaim your agency and refusing the story written for you, because your story was written to change you into a betrayer. So what has to come from who you were before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T16:34:14-07:00","id":576882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=576872#post576872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was a lot more to my post than just that, that I feel addresses most of your response preemptively.<br /> <br /> As well, you'll note I said, &quot;it feels like,&quot; this is what you're saying.<br /> <br /> In the end, I think the key point you're not really addressing is predetermination vs. free-will has a middle ground.<br /> <br /> Background has to impact Seeming, because without background, what defines the character's strengths and weaknesses that in turn define their frame of mind for their choice to escape?<br /> <br /> The issue really can't be that backgrounds are tied heavily into Seeming, because Seeming is so highly based on personality, which is something that comes from background. How do you get to the point of being ready to betray someone to escape your Durance without that part of your personality being there in your background? If your Durance is what makes you like that, then you're not reclaim your agency and refusing the story written for you, because your story was written to change you into a betrayer. So what has to come from who you were before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. IMO, if background and identity doesn't affect your choices, then your choices are arbitrary and random.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T00:07:24-07:00","id":577116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=576882#post576882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. IMO, if background and identity doesn't affect your choices, then your choices are arbitrary and random.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=576872#post576872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the end, I think the key point you're not really addressing is predetermination vs. free-will has a middle ground.<br /> <br /> Background has to impact Seeming, because without background, what defines the character's strengths and weaknesses that in turn define their frame of mind for their choice to escape?</div> </div> </div> </div>As I said in the post on the Wizened thread that led to the creation of this thread. I feel that the current write up places background at 90% influence when I think it should be about 30%. Is 30% sufficiently middle ground for you?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=576872#post576872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you get to the point of being ready to betray someone to escape your Durance without that part of your personality being there in your background?</div> </div> </div> </div> Easily. You have a personality trait like &quot;will betray people to escape torture&quot; (arguably most humans have that trait) but you never noticed it because you were never tortured or at risk of torture before your Durance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=576872#post576872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If your Durance is what makes you like that, then you're not reclaim your agency and refusing the story written for you, because your story was written to change you into a betrayer.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not nessacarally. You're making the assumption that the story was written to change you into a betrayer. That's only true for some Durances; and a Durance can easily turn you into a betrayer even if it wasn't written to do so, even if it was written to do the exact opposite.<br /> <br /> Consider someone who's Durance was being a knight in shining armour, but instead of rescuing the Princess he betrayed her and escaped. That's refusing the story written for you and reclaiming your agency.<br /> <br /> On the other hand if that same person placed into a Game of Thrones/Song of Fire and Ice like Durance then the story would be written to change them into a betrayer; and I do think in that situation it would be significantly harder (but not impossible) to escape as a Darkling.<br /> <br /> Context is key.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-03-2015, 03:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T05:53:32-07:00","id":577279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=577116#post577116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> As I said in the post on the Wizened thread that led to the creation of this thread. I feel that the current write up places background at 90% influence when I think it should be about 30%. Is 30% sufficiently middle ground for you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not even a little. You've made this arbitrary number up (90%), which doesn't actually correlate to the amount of words in the splat writeup in any way, and I don't think most people are getting that read from these writeups. I'm not cutting two-thirds of the words in those writeup; I think I've made this clear a few times already. Also, you want &quot;30%&quot; which is also another arbitrary number. Asking me to do exactly what you want when I've said I might clarify, but am not cutting much of them is not &quot;sufficiently middle ground&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T06:00:47-07:00","id":577281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=576882#post576882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. IMO, if background and identity doesn't affect your choices, then your choices are arbitrary and random.</div> </div> </div> </div>Affect, yes, but not define, and I think the language around that is the sticking point around which this all revolves. Our past informs our future, but it does not dictate it, and I think that distinction is especially significant in terms of an abuse analogy. It does damage to assert to the abused that they are defined more by what happened to them than the choices they make for themselves; those decisions are more defining of a person than their abuse, says more about their demeanor/psychology, and (most importantly) can erupt from many types of backgrounds<br /> <br /> An example: someone abused in a situation that might create an ogre. Pushed far by bullying, that person can break the cycle many ways, perhaps by reacting violently and becoming an ogre, pushing that bully towards someone else and becoming a darkling, or forgiving that person and overcoming it.<br /> <br /> I know the immediate response will be that which of the decisions that person make is defined by how they reacted to that abuse, but I think that is a disservice to the human spirit and to the autonomy with which we are meant to create player characters. I love that the seemings are defined by the manner in which characters seized their own agency. I am disturbed by the implication that they also decide who you were before then and why you needed to at all. I don't think it does damage to the system to suggest they <i>can</i> do so, but that there are other open avenues that are just as valid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5428-mr-feral","name":"Mr. Feral","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5428_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T07:20:40-07:00","id":577319,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr. Feral</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=577281#post577281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am disturbed by the implication that they also decide who you were before then and why you needed to at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I have no idea where that reading comes from. Just because certain backgrounds are more predisposed to react in certain ways, doesn't mean it in any way retroactively determines what your character was like beforehand. <br /> <br /> That's the last post I'm making on this topic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T08:55:43-07:00","id":577392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=577116#post577116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I said in the post on the Wizened thread that led to the creation of this thread. I feel that the current write up places background at 90% influence when I think it should be about 30%. Is 30% sufficiently middle ground for you?</div> </div> </div> </div>You say context is key. These numbers have no context. There's no quantitative metric to go by that I can apply these to. Are you talking word count? Dots on their sheets?<br /> <br /> What's the difference between 75% and 90% influence?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Easily. You have a personality trait like &quot;will betray people to escape torture&quot; (arguably most humans have that trait) but you never noticed it because you were never tortured or at risk of torture before your Durance. </div> </div> </div>So... you're agreeing with me? The Darkling write-up about background is all about people that never noticed their capacity for betrayal, and it takes their Durance to thoroughly break them of that state of denial. The whole point here is that background is what prompts the character traits that lead to escaping a Durance.<br /> <br /> Who you were before your Durance, even if you didn't realize who you really were back then, is what frames your choices that lead to your Seeming.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're making the assumption that the story was written to change you into a betrayer. </div> </div> </div>I'm making the assumption that the change into a betrayer happened for a reason. That reason either had to come from the character, or from the story. If it comes from the character, it must have also come from their background of who they were before this all started. If it comes from the story, it isn't a reclamation of agency.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's only true for some Durances; and a Durance can easily turn you into a betrayer even if it wasn't written to do so, even if it was written to do the exact opposite.<br /> <br /> Consider someone who's Durance was being a knight in shining armour, but instead of rescuing the Princess he betrayed her and escaped. That's refusing the story written for you and reclaiming your agency. </div> </div> </div>Yes, but that requires the knight-in-shining-armor-to-be to have it in them to outright reject this story. If it didn't come from the background of the character, then we have the issue of random/arbitrary actions that make for character that doesn't make any sense.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T10:37:58-07:00","id":577474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=577279#post577279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not even a little. You've made this arbitrary number up (90%), which doesn't actually correlate to the amount of words in the splat writeup in any way, and I don't think most people are getting that read from these writeups. I'm not cutting two-thirds of the words in those writeup; I think I've made this clear a few times already. Also, you want &quot;30%&quot; which is also another arbitrary number. Asking me to do exactly what you want when I've said I might clarify, but am not cutting much of them is not &quot;sufficiently middle ground&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course they're arbitrary. I did say they're entirely my personal feelings, personal feelings are arbitrary.<br /> <br /> I have no idea why you're trying to link &quot;90%&quot; and &quot;30%&quot; to word count, because I never said anything about word count in either this thread nor the wizened thread. &quot;90%&quot; is measures of how much influence I feel the text says your background has on your eventual Seeming; I did say so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=577319#post577319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I have no idea where that reading comes from. Just because certain backgrounds are more predisposed to react in certain ways, doesn't mean it in any way retroactively determines what your character was like beforehand.</div> </div> </div> </div> I point out that the entire purpose of this thread is to explain why I (and hopefully others by extention) are having that reading. If the first post of the thread isn't a sufficent explenation why not ask for expansions and clarifications on the points that aren't clear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=577392#post577392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... you're agreeing with me? The Darkling write-up about background is all about people that never noticed their capacity for betrayal, and it takes their Durance to thoroughly break them of that state of denial.</div> </div> </div> </div> Not really. The Darkling write up says under background that they're powerfully loyal people; I didn't say that example was powerfully loyal. I didn't say anything except typical human nature*.<br /> <br /> * Admittedly I'm not expert on human nature.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=577392#post577392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole point here is that background is what prompts the character traits that lead to escaping a Durance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where as to me the background is not &quot;the whole point&quot;. In fact, the background being &quot;the whole point&quot; is what I specifically disagree with. Other things that matter include:<ul><li>How you're imprisoned. For example - if a key part of your Durance is that you're utterly alone then by definition you can't betray anyone. If you can't betray anyone you can't become a Darkling.</li> <li>Your practical skills. For example - Bob the Accountant notices that his friend is guarding the gate today, surely his friend will let him get close with a knife to escape. But half way there Bob (Suberfuge 0) realises he's covered in sweat and wont fool anyone. He turns back and escapes next month as a Wizened by cooking the books.</li> <li>Blind luck. For example - another True Fae visits your Keeper. Distracted by his guest your Keeper leaves his weapon unattended. Abandoning your plan to build a pair of wings and escape, you take the weapon and wait for your friend to be posted on guard duty.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> And yes, your background is also important. But the current write up, as I explained in the first post, gives me the impression it's almost the only important factor when it should be one of many.<br /> <br /> Background is &quot;not the whole point&quot;. It's an important part of the point, but only part.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=577392#post577392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm making the assumption that the change into a betrayer happened for a reason. That reason either had to come from the character, or from the story. If it comes from the character, it must have also come from their background of who they were before this all started. If it comes from the story, it isn't a reclamation of agency.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's not one or the other. It comes from a combination of background and the story.<br /> <br /> The current write up gives me the feeling that background is all. If you were a bullying victim then you will become an Ogre. I know that MachineIV said this is not true, but him saying that doesn't change the fact the text gives me that impression.<br /> <br /> What I'm saying is that the same person, with the same backstory, can become a different Seeming depending on the escape oppotunities they encounter in their Durance. I know that's how the setting works, and luckily we're going to get a sidebar saying so, but again knowing that doesn't change the impression I get from the text.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=577392#post577392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but that requires the knight-in-shining-armor-to-be to have it in them to outright reject this story. If it didn't come from the background of the character, then we have the issue of random/arbitrary actions that make for character that doesn't make any sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does come from the background. But it also comes from the fact that there was a princess to betray in the first place, the fact that something in the Keeper's domain meant that betraying the princess could lead to your escape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-03-2015, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T10:55:54-07:00","id":577528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=577474#post577474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Background is &quot;not the whole point&quot;. It's an important part of the point, but only part.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, if only the Seeming sections were broken up into different sections based on periods in a changelings life or by general ideas or stuff like that so that readers could delineate one portion of text from the others or something.<br /> <br /> OH WAIT. Background <i>is</i> clearly shown to just be one section of several for the purposes of informing character creation. An important part floating in a setup of other important parts to create a whole.<br /> <br /> Flexible reading takes you far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T10:58:44-07:00","id":577530,"title":"","content":"Arc. I direct you to my first post. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings#post575469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Secondly the way the background flows into the durance, which flows into the escape. The escape That makes perfect sense for an iconic example. If you're the apex of Wizenedness it makes sense your key life events are all Wizenedly - but the iconic example is also the only example in the seeming text; and it uses terms like &quot;Before the Durance, many Wizened&quot; - which while clearly stating that it's not all Wizened - also clearly state that it is not one single example.<br /> <br /> The example's pomimence and it's explicit plurality gives me an impression that the iconic example is also the default example; and in the default example the Escape flows directly from the Background.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=577528#post577528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Flexible reading takes you far.</div> </div> </div> </div>Different people are different. I'm a less flexible reader than you, that doesn't mean my reading or the emotional reaction I have is less valid than yours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-03-2015, 02:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T23:49:23-07:00","id":578323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=577474#post577474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no idea why you're trying to link &quot;90%&quot; and &quot;30%&quot; to word count,...</div> </div> </div> </div>Because you're not providing a context for what those numbers mean. 90% isn't a feeling. It's a quantitative statement. You can't quantify feelings. You can't effectively communicate your issue with how influential backgrounds are if you continue to rely on terminology that communicates nothing of substance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not really. The Darkling write up says under background that they're powerfully loyal people; I didn't say that example was powerfully loyal. I didn't say anything except typical human nature*. </div> </div> </div>This response doesn't make any sense with what was said in the previous two posts in question.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Where as to me the background is not &quot;the whole point&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Seriously stop.<br /> <br /> If we're going to talk about this, you need to address what I'm saying in good faith.<br /> <br /> The fact that I used the words, &quot;background,&quot; &quot;whole,&quot; and &quot;point,&quot; does not mean, &quot;I think background is the whole point.&quot; I said, &quot;The whole point here is that background is what prompts the character traits that lead to escaping a Durance.&quot; Which is a fundamentally different statement.<br /> <br /> At this point it very much feels like you've decided that since I disagree with you, you're allowed to argue whatever you want regardless of what I said and treat it as direct discussion, or just make things up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How you're imprisoned. For example - if a key part of your Durance is that you're utterly alone then by definition you can't betray anyone. If you can't betray anyone you can't become a Darkling. </div> </div> </div>I don't really imagine a Changeling tossed into an empty abyss (or endless whiteness) of nothingness to escape. I don't really see it being a Durance at all, because why would one of the Gentry nab you solely to shove you into a realm of pure nothingness?<br /> <br /> Beyond the issue what that example, yes, there's no issue with Durance mattering. Durances are going to lend themselves to certain Seemings. But a Durance that presents the chance for betrayal doesn't make a changeling into a Darkling. Their choice to go against the story are betray does. And that choice has to have its beginnings in their background.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your practical skills. </div> </div> </div>It's pretty clear (since 1e) that Arcadia doesn't operate on normal logic and your character's &quot;sheet&quot; before they were taken doesn't actually dictated what they can and can't do in the narrative run logic of a Durance.<br /> <br /> As well, those practical skills are an extension of your background anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Blind luck. For example - another True Fae visits your Keeper. Distracted by his guest your Keeper leaves his weapon unattended. Abandoning your plan to build a pair of wings and escape, you take the weapon and wait for your friend to be posted on guard duty. </div> </div> </div>Blind luck should be irrelevant to your Seeming beyond the circumstances of your escape; or perhaps result in no Seeming. Blind luck isn't regaining agency.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And yes, your background is also important. But the current write up, as I explained in the first post, gives me the impression it's almost the only important factor when it should be one of many. </div> </div> </div>You haven't really expressed why that should be taken as more than just a subjective impression that may or may not be reasonably derived from the text in the abstract.<br /> <br /> Background is first, and prominent, because it frames the other factors. It presents the traits you have before that guide your character's actions during their Duration. It represents the emotional anchor point of agency that was lost and what resonates with your character to regain it. It is the starting factor from which the others derive or respond to; hence the importance placed on it in the text.<br /> <br /> Stating the text presents it as the &quot;only important factor&quot; is easily disproved. You bring up the need of others to betray to become a Darkling. That means the circumstances of your Durance absolutely matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not one or the other. It comes from a combination of background and the story. </div> </div> </div>I said &quot;or&quot; for a reason.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I know that MachineIV said this is not true, but him saying that doesn't change the fact the text gives me that impression. </div> </div> </div>And I still don't think even with all your posts here you're really expanding beyond that in a meaningful fashion. You're managed to say, &quot;it gives me this impression&quot; with a lot more words, but not necessarily any more clarity as to the source of the problem beyond the idea that you're comparing how CtL 2e is written to how other WOD books are written on the subject. But even that doesn't actually address what's wrong with the text for you, just preconceptions you're bringing to the table.<br /> <br /> You've acknowledged that background should influence the rest, but are then trying to make an argument for it having too much influence, without even address what too much is, or what less is, or what the right amount is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What I'm saying is that the same person, with the same backstory, can become a different Seeming depending on the escape oppotunities they encounter in their Durance. </div> </div> </div>This should be a maybe at best though. If the backstory just doesn't support the actions needed to get to a specific Seeming even if the Durance makes that Seeming a possibility, it shouldn't happen. Some characters combined with a variety of choices should have a variety of possible Seemings. Other characters shouldn't because their characterization only really leads to one avenue of meaningful rebellion against the narrative controlling them leading to either never escaping (remember that's supposed to happen plenty, we just don't play those) or a specific Seeming. If anybody can become any Seeming with the right circumstances, then the emotional impact of regaining agency is lessened because it isn't personalized; it stops being about really regaining agency in a personally significant fashion, and simply becomes rebelling against the narrative of the Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T01:03:31-07:00","id":578383,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=578323#post578323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You haven't really expressed why that should be taken as more than just a subjective impression that may or may not be reasonably derived from the text in the abstract.</div> </div> </div> </div> I <u><b>never said</b></u> it was anything other than my subjective impression.<br /> <br /> The entire reason people asked me to create this thread is because they wished to know more about the thoughts that led to my subjective impression.<br /> <br /> As for whether it's &quot;reasonable&quot;. Define reasonable. People were interested in what went on inside my head, I wrote a post to answer their questions. It got a fair number of likes, I've seen some complaints about Background being too restrictive on RPG.net so presumably it's not just me off in cloud cookoo land.<br /> <br /> (I'm moving this to the top because it's a key point.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=578323#post578323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because you're not providing a context for what those numbers mean.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually I did.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Myself, in the post that led to people asking for this thread</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's really quite simple. I feel that who you were before your durance should be about 30% of the influence on your eventual seeming; with the form of your durance and whatever escape oppotunities present themselves being the other 70%. The current write up feels more like it's 90% background.</div> </div> </div> </div>That looks like pretty clear context to me. It's the relavitve importance of your life pre-Arcadia against other factors; not word count.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=578323#post578323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">90% isn't a feeling. It's a quantitative statement. You can't quantify feelings.</div> </div> </div> </div> Sure you can.<br /> <br /> &quot;I fell Jar Jar Binks made the Phantom Menace a worse film&quot; is a very common thing to say. &quot;I feel Jar Jar Binks made the Phantom Menace 50% worse&quot; is unusual phrasing, but just as valid.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=578323#post578323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You can't effectively communicate your issue with how influential backgrounds are if you continue to rely on terminology that communicates nothing of substance.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm not <i>relying</i> on that terminology. Quite the opposite, &quot;90%&quot; was just me stating what I feel.<br /> <br /> The actual explenation of why I feel what I feel, the entire purpose, of this thread is in the first post of this thread. You'll notice I don't use percentages once in the thread's first post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=578323#post578323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This response doesn't make any sense with what was said in the previous two posts in question.</div> </div> </div> </div> I makes sense to me. You asked if I agreed with you, and then imediately connected your statement to the Darkling write up. Thus your statement became &quot;did you just agree with me, and thus by extention did you just agree with the Darkling write up&quot;. To which I pointed out I didn't just agree with the Darkling write up because I didn't say anything about loyalty.<br /> <br /> That might not be what you intended but that's how I read it.<br /> <br /> If you meant to ask &quot;did you just agree that your example charachter escaped because of an aspect of his backstory - &quot;he is willing to betray people to escape torture but never knew it&quot;. Then I would reply:<br /> <br /> I agreed with that from the start. It's the now infamous &quot;30%&quot;, but I still consider the fact that this example charachter had the oppotunity to escape via betrayal a more important factor than his backstory. He, due to being a minimal example, was a charachter that was equally pre-disposed to being any Seeming so his opportunities were what mattered.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=578323#post578323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I said, &quot;The whole point here is that background is what prompts the character traits that lead to escaping a Durance.&quot; Which is a fundamentally different statement.</div> </div> </div> </div> And that is exactly what I replied too.<br /> <br /> I do not think it's &quot;character traits that lead to escaping a Durance&quot;. I think charachter traits are important, and that background leads to charachter traits*. But they're not the only important thing or even the most important thing - that's why I gave a list of other things I consider important.<br /> <br /> * But not all of them. Kith provides charachter traits, and if you define background as &quot;pre-Aracdia&quot; you also have pre-escape charachter development in Arcadia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=578323#post578323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's pretty clear (since 1e) that Arcadia doesn't operate on normal logic and your character's &quot;sheet&quot; before they were taken doesn't actually dictated what they can and can't do in the narrative run logic of a Durance.</div> </div> </div> </div> I disagree. Arcadia runs on story-logic; most stories contain the concept of charachter skill levels.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=578323#post578323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blind luck should be irrelevant to your Seeming beyond the circumstances of your escape; or perhaps result in no Seeming. Blind luck isn't regaining agency.</div> </div> </div> </div> Blind luck can't give you agency.<br /> <br /> Blind luck can give you opportunity. Choosing to take advantage of opportunity gives you agency.<br /> <br /> That's why I specifically crafted an example to show a charachter displaying agency that flows from the oppotuntiy created by blind luck.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=578323#post578323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And I still don't think even with all your posts here you're really expanding beyond that in a meaningful fashion. You're managed to say, &quot;it gives me this impression&quot; with a lot more words, but not necessarily any more clarity as to the source of the problem beyond the idea that you're comparing how CtL 2e is written to how other WOD books are written on the subject. But even that doesn't actually address what's wrong with the text for you, just preconceptions you're bringing to the table.</div> </div> </div> </div> Of course it does. I point you to the thread title. People asked me why I feel what I feel. This thread is about my preconceptions and other feelings first and the text itself only by extension.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I thought that first post made it pretty obvious what's wrong with the text for me but if you'd like me to state so explicitly its:<ul><li>Uses what I consider to be technical terms for Splat write ups in non-standard ways: &quot;Background&quot; as part of an 'iconic example' rather than for general trends on where the splat comes from.</li> <li>Information vital to all Changelings such as what you actually do to gain the Seeming is only given as part of the 'iconic example'.</li> <li>No discussion of escapes that have a root in anything other than your pre-Arcadia life; such as escapes that have a root in your Keeper's weakness.</li> </ul><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=578323#post578323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This should be a maybe at best though. If the backstory just doesn't support the actions needed to get to a specific Seeming even if the Durance makes that Seeming a possibility, it shouldn't happen.</div> </div> </div> </div> On this I strongly strongly disagree. It should be a more than a maybe.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that anybody can become any seeming. I'm saying that any well rounded human being has the potential for at least three of the six primary Seemings. Someone who only has the potential to become one Seeming would be a rare fringe case like an autistic savant. (Actually I could see savants becoming a Beast almost as easily as a Wizened).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-04-2015, 04:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T07:06:31-07:00","id":578690,"title":"","content":"I find it highly amusing that in a thread that's supposed to be clarifying why you find something unclear, any attempt to point out that it isn't actually all that clarifying or clear is being treated with fairly obnoxious bad faith arguments that seem to only have the purpose of making any such critiques look bad so your own issuing with communicating your ideas clearly don't need to be examined.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 07-04-2015, 12:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T08:05:21-07:00","id":578765,"title":"","content":"So, it's taken me a while to figure out how exactly I want to express my response, but here's my own feelings on the matter.<br /> <br /> Seeming in 1e said little to nothing about who your character was. It was a vehicle for delivering a set of affinity contracts attached to a superficial description of how it made your character look. As an afterthought, it also gave a reason people of that seeming were usually taken (lured into the wild for Beasts, as punishment for some unknown transgression for Darklings, specifically desired by their furure Keeper for Elementals, coveted for their beauty and skill for Fairest, used as a weapon for Ogres, and no reason at all for Wizened). Most people I played with ignored that part anyway. As a result, characters were often extremely superficial, i.e. &quot;I'm a Dual-Kith something something of the whatever court&quot; with no further explanation. The reason, I feel, that the sample backgrounds in 2e are so detailed and specifically tied into the character's escape is to get people thinking about the character as a person with a history that lead them to become who they are today, not just a collection of superficial traits. Don't just tell me what your character looks like, tell me a story about who they were before, why they were taken, and how their life experiences lead them to their escape. It doesn't have to be the same story that the Seeming's write up tells; that should go without saying. I want to hear <i>your</i> character's story, but I want that story to tell me something about who your character is and how they got to be that way. The sample backgrounds and escapes, to me, are just examples of what a good character background should look like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T09:20:22-07:00","id":578865,"title":"","content":"Well Charlaquin, I can't really disagree with that. Whether or not this was the author's intent, well I won't speculate on that. My own experience of 1E charachter creation at the table sounds like it was more positive than yours - but that's just my experience.<br /> <br /> I can say that if you're correct about the intent I can see how that would lead to the discord I'm seeing. In setting a Seeming is created by one specific decision, while your talking about them as the seed for an entire life; before and after that decision. Naturally they'd be friction between &quot;one decision&quot; and &quot;a whole lifetime&quot;, and it seems I'm particularly sensitive to that friction.<br /> <br /> <br /> And Heavy Arms. Given that your criticisms with my communication include things like my attempt to explain my subjective feelings not having an explanation why it should be taken as anything more than subjective; well you'll have to fogrive me if I don't take your latest ad-hominem that seriously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T10:02:12-07:00","id":578901,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I definitely don't know if it's specifically the author's or developer's intent, but it's one of the most appealing features for me that Seemings have detailed example backgrounds.<br /> <br /> I've had good and bad experiences with Changeling character creation, but the good ones always told a story including who they were before they were taken, how and why they were taken, what they were made to do during their Durance, and how and why they escaped. Unfortunately, more often I just saw detailed descriptions of character appearance with a slapped together background that was mostly there to justify why they looked the way they did. These new Seemings write ups all tell stories, and the kind of stories that I've seen lead to well-developed, interesting Changeling characters.<br /> <br /> I'm thrilled that Seeming will mean something more than just an archetype, and that there are robust examples to draw from for players who may not be used to thinking about their Changeling characters in that way. So hopefully you'll understand why I find it so disheartening to see so many people object to the detailed example backgrounds.<br /> <br /> While I too find the the percent values somewhat arbitrary, I actually don't disagree with the underlying impression that background is an extremely significant determining factor in what Seeming a character ends up in. I just don't think that the character's background has to cleave to the examples. Past experiences help shape characters, Changeling or otherwise. Ultimately, a character's Seeming comes down to how they escaped, but that decision should make sense for the character, and when writing your character's background, you should consider how it may have lead up to your character's capture and their escape.<br /> <br /> That's my 2 cents, anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 07-04-2015, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T10:28:16-07:00","id":578923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=578865#post578865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Heavy Arms. Given that your criticisms with my communication include things like my attempt to explain my subjective feelings not having an explanation why it should be taken as anything more than subjective; well you'll have to fogrive me if I don't take your latest ad-hominem that seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given you're repeated insistence on not responding to what I've typed and manufacturing strawmen to beat up, and &quot;ooh you can say ad hominem I'm impressed,&quot; I'm at least very clear that at leat 90% of your problems with the Seemings in 2e has nothing to do with what's actually written and is all about what you've decided in your head is there despite the text being open for everyone to see.<br /> <br /> Snipping my quotes out of context and rearranging my phrasings into different meanings does not demonstrate your ability to critically read a passage. It strongly demonstrates you getting defensive that your explanation isn't actually that good of one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T10:31:50-07:00","id":578925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=578901#post578901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So hopefully you'll understand why I find it so disheartening to see so many people object to the detailed example backgrounds.</div> </div> </div> </div> I certainly understand more than I did yesterday <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I still disagree with you, I still but even just knowing about your past experiences at the table makes it easier to understand where you're coming from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=578901#post578901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I too find the the percent values somewhat arbitrary, I actually don't disagree with the underlying impression that background is an extremely significant determining factor in what Seeming a character ends up in.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm not going to deny it; they are arbitary. Those percentages are a description of my feelings, and feeling often are somewhat arbitary. Though it is nice to hear you agree about the underlying impression <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-04-2015, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T14:49:13-07:00","id":579150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=577474#post577474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I point out that the entire purpose of this thread is to explain why I (and hopefully others by extention) are having that reading. If the first post of the thread isn't a sufficent explenation why not ask for expansions and clarifications on the points that aren't clear.</div> </div> </div> </div>+1, Agree and all that jazz.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T15:06:10-07:00","id":579180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=579150#post579150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> +1, Agree and all that jazz.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably could have just used the &quot;Like&quot; button to express that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T21:10:30-07:00","id":579427,"title":"","content":"So people's history with things, being different from other peoples' history, can alter how they interpret things and make decisions about them? Strange. Almost as if someone's background has an affect on the choices they make later about things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/137x125q90/745/a5GS5M.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/802-amaterasu","name":"amaterasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"208"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T21:39:42-07:00","id":579440,"title":"","content":"While I don't think it's quite as bad, it does feel like the narrative weight of the escape is crushed by the importance of a character's personal history in terms of text and tone.<br /> <br /> But really, I think this will just get dismissed and ignored because it's 'not reading flexibly/critically enough' again so it's not really worth wasting any more air on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1462,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","user":"Xenesis","date":". 07-05-2015, 12:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T21:49:33-07:00","id":579446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=579440#post579440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But really, I think this will just get dismissed as 'not reading flexibly/critically enough' again so it's not really worth wasting any more air on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The next time somebody calls me passive-aggressive (and it has been a hot minute), I am pointing to this.<br /> <br /> Any waste of internet-air that a hypothetical elaboration would have cost you has been significantly multiplied by instead opting to lament the fact that people got annoyed with you for bogging down an earlier discussion with metaconversation about reactions to exasperating behaviors endemic to the fandom.<br /> <br /> By all means, share how you suppose the aforementioned distribution of narrative weight happens or might be remedied. It would be eminently preferable to hear about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T22:10:54-07:00","id":579463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=579440#post579440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I don't think it's quite as bad, it does feel like the narrative weight of the escape is crushed by the importance of a character's personal history in terms of text and tone.<br /> <br /> But really, I think this will just get dismissed and ignored because it's 'not reading flexibly/critically enough' again so it's not really worth wasting any more air on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, either you think that there's a real majority on this point, or you place a lot of weight in the words of a few people saying this. Maybe you wanna reconsider the import you're giving this differing opinion? Unless you for some reason think the opinion expressed has weight because it lines up with the writers and developers, but that's another can of worms.<br /> <br /> Putting that aside, I can say that personally, the main thing I remember from the Seemings is the nature of their choices. Like, it seriously takes me a few seconds to remember backgrounds when this conversation comes up. If people want to argue about the nature of the choices being restrictive, I'd get that, though I still lean more towards the current write up.<br /> <br /> See, for the core, you need something lean, some sharp, something definite-something that sparks character ideas, gives a clear vision and direction. I feel like the core does that in the same way Blood and Smoke, Demon, Beast, and Idigam did. Now, in supplemental materials? If I were writing stuff on Seemings? You bet, I'd explore all the crevices of the implied archetype I had word count for, both on backgrounds and escape. I'd come up with new varitions on the curses and blessings for each, even.** I think the archetypes have room to be explored. But for the core, with so much being brought in and updated, I want the clear vision.<br /> <br /> I know people have players who hew closely to the text and think that limits them. But I'm willing to wager the greater majority of people will either appreciate the direction or know enough to play around with the idea to not be limited by it. This has been my experience at the table, this has been my experience in play. Hell, this is my experience <i>preparing for a playtest of this game now. </i>So I'm not interested in having Lost pander to a crowd who seems to be a minimal sum from what I've seen.<br /> <br /> Maybe your experience at the table has been different?*<br /> <br /> *I freely admit this is a pointed statement. I'm done talking hypotheticals when I'm running games.<br /> **I have now actually written a loose outline of how I would, in fact, arrange such sections in supplements, with some broad strokes on direction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-05-2015, 01:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T23:15:24-07:00","id":579498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=579446#post579446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The next time somebody calls me passive-aggressive (and it has been a hot minute), I am pointing to this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please do. It's a stellar example of such and I won't say otherwise. I'm frustrated and I'm venting. I felt being passive aggressive was better than being aggressive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=579463#post579463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[snip]<br /> Maybe your experience at the table has been different?*</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that the people I do game with are majority literal minded people, yes, my experience has been largely different. Considering I have spent hundreds and hundreds of hours editing a 300-page document so there's almost no possible way anything could be misconstrued, yes. Considering I've read thousands of scientific papers, comprehending and analysing them yes. I have been trained by a decade of professional experience to read and interpret what I'm reading in a literal sense.<br /> <br /> I game with a lot of people who have done/do similar. I have seen arguments at games I've been at that people aren't playing X court or whatever because it's too far out of what the idea proposed by the books are. I have experienced interactions that have required mediation because someone was using the canon as a cudgel to damage people's character concepts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> **I have now actually written a loose outline of how I would, in fact, arrange such sections in supplements, with some broad strokes on direction. </div> </div> </div>That's great and all, but the foundation is the foundation and informs the entire game. The foundation wants us to typecast our characters (in some seemings more, some less). Either way, I don't have the resolve for any more on this. No doubt you're finding me tedious, so I'll go on my 'inflexible' way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T23:27:40-07:00","id":579502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=579498#post579498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's great and all, but the foundation is the foundation and informs the entire game. The foundation wants us to typecast our characters (in some seemings more, some less). Either way, I don't have the resolve for any more on this. No doubt you're finding me tedious, so I'll go on my 'inflexible' way.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's more coming, because I do want to respond to certain things, but I want one thing out here:<br /> <br /> Xen, I'm not seeing eye to eye with you, but you are the not the one I feel is inflexible here. I have seen you be flexible in the <i>freaking Beast threads</i>, which is a god damned minefield of people not getting the idea. I can see you getting the point I and others are making while still keeping the opposite stance.That's <i>fine</i>. There are others here who are way less flexible than you, and it's to them my comments are usually aimed at.<br /> <br /> My current problem is that you seem inclined to think that I (and others) am out to get you. Maybe this is the result of my trying to play nice as I'm getting involved with a thread I admittedly have antipathy for and not specifying who is aggravating me. I just kind of speak to a general crowd, and if you think you're in that crowd, you get hurt. I don't want to start calling people out and instead just kind of speak broadly, but I will say this: of all the people I am admonishing to read more broadly, you were not on the list of people I was thinking of. Like, at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T00:03:48-07:00","id":579547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=579498#post579498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that the people I do game with are majority literal minded people, yes, my experience has been largely different. Considering I have spent hundreds and hundreds of hours editing a 300-page document so there's almost no possible way anything could be misconstrued, yes. Considering I've read thousands of scientific papers, comprehending and analysing them yes. I have been trained by a decade of professional experience to read and interpret what I'm reading in a literal sense.<br /> <br /> I game with a lot of people who have done/do similar. I have seen arguments at games I've been at that people aren't playing X court or whatever because it's too far out of what the idea proposed by the books are. I have experienced interactions that have required mediation because someone was using the canon as a cudgel to damage people's character concepts.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) So what you're saying is that your extensive background with a particular style of work and a particular set of people has led you to see things in a certain way and respond accordingly with particular kinds of choices? Like, there's a relation between your background and how you enact agency?(Okay, I'm sorry, that's me being an ass, but the parallel was begging to be pointed out. I freely admit to being an immature snot at times.)<br /> <br /> 2) Okay, so <i>yes</i>, you have a totally different experience from me at the table. Cool. So now we're at a point where we both have to acknowledge the limits of our perspective.<br /> <br /> I'll freely admit, I don't read a lot of Actual Plays, so I can only speculate about what the majority of gamers experience at the table based on my experiences with people on the forums, and that's mixed by a lot of factors.. I have no idea if you read them or not, nor will I begin to speculate about what your take away from the populace is.<br /> <br /> <i>That said</i>, I'm willing to bet David, at least, <i>has</i> gotten a broad perspective. Again, his attitude is not to just assume things are good and represent the same old things with shiny, barely updated mechanics. I know for a fact his own play experience influences his designs, because he talks fairly regularly about it, but I also know the guy reads and researches other games. He talks about trends he has seen quite frequently as well. The design direction that Seemings go are done as a response to that, and I think it speaks to both his preferences and what his research yields.<br /> <br /> Maybe I idly trust him because his modus operandi of direction lines up neatly with my own experience, because the suggested writing plays to my biases. I admit that. Maybe he's way off base. I have trouble buying that for various reasons, but again, maybe I'm biased.<br /> <br /> But is it that much of a stretch that this is written in such a way because the people writing this see things a different way than we do? I mean, I'll tell you something: even as a playtester, you see things differently than you did as a normal player. Seeing the raw text and how it gets polished up changes your perspective on how to respond to it and how to respond to people who haven't seen the things you have. And that's just one layer of difference of involvement with the text and the project. A dev is at least three layers removed from the average reader/players perspective in response to their responsibilities.<br /> <br /> At what point in this discussion do we stop trusting that the devs are doing these things for reasons that make sense from their higher perspective and start assuming they're missing things on the small scale? I don't know, but I don't think we've passed that point. A lot of people here clearly feel like we have. Again, there's probably a lot of bias is playing out here on both sides.<br /> <br /> But again, my problem was made in a much angrier post some ways back. At this point, we know what's going to be done, and all we can do is wait to see how the decisions pan out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-05-2015, 03:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T00:09:15-07:00","id":579550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amaterasu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=579427#post579427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So people's history with things, being different from other peoples' history, can alter how they interpret things and make decisions about them? Strange. Almost as if someone's background has an affect on the choices they make later about things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody's saying or said otherwise.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T02:05:26-07:00","id":579650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=579440#post579440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But really, I think this will just get dismissed and ignored because it's 'not reading flexibly/critically enough' again so it's not really worth wasting any more air on it.</div> </div> </div> </div>FYI, this thread has already gotten the developer to promise to devote word count to addressing the issue. It was post #7.<br /> <br /> (Also, the air is just for cooling purposes; what you're wasting is electrons. I mean, literally speaking. Metaphorically literally speaking.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T05:47:34-07:00","id":579735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=579180#post579180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably could have just used the &quot;Like&quot; button to express that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah. The like button doesn't show who is agreeing, it just shows that someone liked it. Additionally, I don't want to +1 every single post he has made in this thread so far.<br /> <br /> I get the &quot;Fight with tooth and claw&quot;-impression ALOT on these forums, more than any other forums I visit regularily actually (several different roleplaying sites and reddit), in particular when it comes to &quot;defending&quot; the creation that is being put out. It's almost as if the people who put out the work more want a pat on their ego when they are offering it for review than actually wanting feedback that might critizise their creative decisions. Which is fine, by the way, but then it shouldn't be called out for discussion.<br /> <a href=\"http://goinswriter.com/the-difference-between-good-writers-and-bad-writers/\" target=\"_blank\">Not a lot of writers do call out for feedback during their creative work, because generally someone somewhere will shoot it down, rightfully or not, and as a result, they might come to ignore all feedback that doesn't suite them, creating a barrier that halts your creative work because you are mad at someone for saying that they didn't like what you produced.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T07:38:03-07:00","id":579811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Errol216</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=579650#post579650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">FYI, this thread has already gotten the developer to promise to devote word count to addressing the issue. It was post #7.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was definitely not this thread that got David to devote wordcount to clarifying that the backgrounds are examples. He's been saying he would clarify that since this whole argument was first raised in the Darkling thread. This horse has been dead for a long, long time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T12:24:19-07:00","id":580058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=579811#post579811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was definitely not this thread that got David to devote wordcount to clarifying that the backgrounds are examples. He's been saying he would clarify that since this whole argument was first raised in the Darkling thread. This horse has been dead for a long, long time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Other things this thread has established: how bad my memory is. -_-","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T14:40:38-07:00","id":581555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=579735#post579735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get the &quot;Fight with tooth and claw&quot;-impression ALOT on these forums, more than any other forums I visit regularily actually (several different roleplaying sites and reddit), in particular when it comes to &quot;defending&quot; the creation that is being put out. It's almost as if the people who put out the work more want a pat on their ego when they are offering it for review than actually wanting feedback that might critizise their creative decisions. Which is fine, by the way, but then it shouldn't be called out for discussion.<br /> Not a lot of writers do call out for feedback during their creative work, because generally someone somewhere will shoot it down, rightfully or not, and as a result, they might come to ignore all feedback that doesn't suite them, creating a barrier that halts your creative work because you are mad at someone for saying that they didn't like what you produced.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're being a bit uncharitable. I think that the Onyx Path writers do value and made use of the feedback they get - after all, they're not really under any onus to take feedback at all, as you pointed out, and if they're looking for undiluted adulation, the internet <i>really</i> isn't the place to go for that.<br /> <br /> However, there's a difference between saying &quot;I don't think you expressed this clearly&quot; or &quot;I'm not sure the theme is coming across in this particular spot&quot; and saying &quot;I don't like this new direction at all because [blank].&quot; That's generally not constructive criticism. Maybe if a large majority of people had the same reaction, it might make the writers reconsider the project, but probably not even then, since it's not like they can just start re-writing the whole thing from scratch at this point in development.<br /> <br /> When the writers come forward to &quot;defend&quot; their work, it usually seems to be in response to this kind of feedback. I'm not a mind-reader, but I think what they're doing is basically trying to persuade people to keep an open mind about the changes they're making. I mean really, if somebody complains about something that you can't really change, what's there to to but try and convince them that it's still something they can enjoy?<br /> <br /> Also, if you really think that Onyx Path is full of bad writers, why do you even care enough to comment on their forums?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 07-06-2015, 05:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T15:32:04-07:00","id":581577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=579735#post579735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nah. The like button doesn't show who is agreeing, it just shows that someone liked it. Additionally, I don't want to +1 every single post he has made in this thread so far.<br /> <br /> I get the &quot;Fight with tooth and claw&quot;-impression ALOT on these forums, more than any other forums I visit regularily actually (several different roleplaying sites and reddit), in particular when it comes to &quot;defending&quot; the creation that is being put out. <b>It's almost as if the people who put out the work more want a pat on their ego</b> when they are offering it for review than actually wanting feedback that might critizise their creative decisions. Which is fine, by the way, but then it shouldn't be called out for discussion.<br /> <a href=\"http://goinswriter.com/the-difference-between-good-writers-and-bad-writers/\" target=\"_blank\">Not a lot of writers do call out for feedback during their creative work, because generally someone somewhere will shoot it down, rightfully or not, and as a result, they might come to ignore all feedback that doesn't suite them, creating a barrier that halts your creative work because you are mad at someone for saying that they didn't like what you produced.</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I just want to comment on this. This is, of course, based on my own experience which I have no way of validating sans a lot of asking and waiting for material to come out, so feel free to be skeptical.<br /> <br /> That said, the bolded is untrue. Flatly. I have been approached by several friends who are also writers for Onyx Path to read their material before sending it out, and they have all told me that if I tell them that it's fine as it is, they will slap me upside the head. I am not friends with every writer for Onyx Path, but the group I'm with has never been satisfied with a pat on the back. Some of them are, in fact, really paranoid about such responses.<br /> <br /> There are any number of people who they can go to just give them idle praise. There are also tons of people willing to nitpick a piece into oblivion. Neither is hard to find. What writers are looking for in feedback is a willingness to understand the destination they want their work to arrive at and some good dialogue on how to keep the direction straight for it.<br /> <br /> We as a fanbase should ask of writers where they are going and why they think the pieces they produce go there. We can think the destination is wrong, we can even say that, but theres' no point in harping on about it, and once we give that bit of honest truth, we should talk with them and help them figure out how to bring about the vision they have. Maybe in the process, we'll even change our minds. Maybe we won't.<br /> <br /> But the key thing here is that this isn't just a simple case of &quot;You're supposed to give us what we want, why aren't you doing that?&quot; It's <i>always</i> a dialogue, it's <i>always </i>a discussion, and it involves respecting the fact that sometimes a writer is going to go to New York when you might want to go to San Francisco, as much as they need to respectfully think on your input to go by way of Philadelphia rather than Cleveland.<br /> <br /> Or something, I've only been to Florida in terms of the Eastern US.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, in the end, yes, I am of the opinion that ultimately, the devs and writers are the ones driving the car, rather than the audience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T09:09:01-07:00","id":582411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=581555#post581555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, if you really think that Onyx Path is full of bad writers, why do you even care enough to comment on their forums?</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the feeling you might have not have read a single thing I actually have written on this forum, not even the post you replied to, or decided that what I actually wrote meant something else.<br /> This is exactly what I mean with tooth and claw attitude. &quot;Someone said something bad about my precious game?! They must be stupid and shouldn't even be here!!!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanearts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=581555#post581555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, in the end, yes, I am of the opinion that ultimately, the devs and writers are the ones driving the car, rather than the audience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely so. I'll even like your comment for the several good points you made. Cheers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T09:26:27-07:00","id":582428,"title":"","content":"Thank you very much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T11:19:59-07:00","id":582533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>A_Newfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/575469-why-i-feel-like-backgrounds-are-the-primary-criteria-for-seemings?p=582411#post582411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get the feeling you might have not have read a single thing I actually have written on this forum, not even the post you replied to, or decided that what I actually wrote meant something else.<br /> This is exactly what I mean with tooth and claw attitude. &quot;Someone said something bad about my precious game?! They must be stupid and shouldn't even be here!!!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You are correct in that I didn't go out of my way to track down your other comments; I was responding only to this one specifically. I apologize if I misunderstood your intent; allow me to explain why I thought you were accusing Onyx Path of being full of bad writers:<br /> <br /> Firstly, you write &quot;It's almost as if the people who put out the work more want a pat on their ego when they are offering it for review than actually wanting feedback that might critizise their creative decisions,&quot; with regard to the people who contribute to &quot;these forums.&quot; I took this to be an accusation against the Onyx Path writers, since they're the ones who offer samples of their writing for review on these forums<br /> <br /> Secondly, you write &quot;Not a lot of writers do call out for feedback during their creative work, because generally someone somewhere will shoot it down, rightfully or not, and as a result, they might come to ignore all feedback that doesn't suite them, creating a barrier that halts your creative work because you are mad at someone for saying that they didn't like what you produced.&quot; Based on your previous statement, you appear to be claiming that the Onyx Path writers have established such a creative barrier through rejecting any feedback that isn't &quot;patting their ego.&quot;<br /> <br /> Thirdly, you linked the above statement to an article entitled &quot;The Difference Between Good Writers and Bad Writers,&quot; which states that, among other things, the ability to graciously accept criticism is what separates good writers from bad writers. Based on your previous statements, it appears that you are saying that the Onyx Path writers, being people who do not accept negative feedback, would fall into the category of &quot;bad writers.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Hopefully that clarifies where I'm coming from, and confirms to your satisfaction that I did, in fact, read your post. I think, upon further review, that you may have been trying to accuse the other commenters on this site of misunderstanding the writers' intentions when it comes to seeking feedback and &quot;defending&quot; their work instead of contributing to the discussion. However, if this is the case, I hope you can understand why your statement was easy to misinterpret.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 07-07-2015, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T11:34:09-07:00","id":582543,"title":"","content":"And thank you as well, Cat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}